WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.796
Wendy was brought up to the deck of the Jolly Roger

2
00:00:03.797 --> 00:00:08.855
. The boys were lined up in their chains trying to look

3
00:00:08.856 --> 00:00:14.011
brave. When she saw the pirates preparing the plank, she was filled with

4
00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:18.005
hate. She hated Hook and she hated the

5
00:00:18.006 --> 00:00:23.678
pirates. Boys might think pirates exciting, but Wendy did

6
00:00:23.679 --> 00:00:28.345
not. She especially hated that the ship had not been cleaned for

7
00:00:28.346 --> 00:00:32.195
years. Not one window was without a layer of

8
00:00:32.196 --> 00:00:39.012
grime. In fact, while she was below, she wrote "Dirty Pig" on a window with her

9
00:00:39.013 --> 00:00:44.438
finger. She also hated that it was nighttime and no one was in

10
00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:49.795
bed. But when the boys gathered around her, all these thoughts melted

11
00:00:49.796 --> 00:00:57.397
away. "So, my beauty," said Hook, "soon you will see your children walk the

12
00:00:57.398 --> 00:01:03.651
plank." Hook’s lace collar was dirty, and when he saw Wendy staring, he tried to hide

13
00:01:03.652 --> 00:01:08.827
it. "Are the children going to die?" she asked

14
00:01:08.828 --> 00:01:13.268
scornfully. Her voice made it clear how she despised Hook for his

15
00:01:13.269 --> 00:01:22.087
plan. "They are!" he shouted. "Silence! Listen to a mother’s last words to her

16
00:01:22.088 --> 00:01:26.277
children." Wendy stood tall and faced everyone

17
00:01:26.278 --> 00:01:30.469
proudly. "These are my last words, dear boys," she

18
00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:33.796
said. "I feel that your real mothers would say

19
00:01:33.797 --> 00:01:38.078
this: We hope our sons die like

20
00:01:38.079 --> 00:01:46.515
gentlemen." Hook shuddered. Even the pirates were awed, for Wendy’s words were the kind that inspired

21
00:01:46.516 --> 00:01:51.706
bravery. Tootles cried out, "I am going to do what my mother

22
00:01:51.707 --> 00:01:55.074
wishes. What are you going to do,

23
00:01:55.075 --> 00:02:01.507
Slightly?" "What my mother wishes," said Slightly. "What are you going to do,

24
00:02:01.508 --> 00:02:07.506
Nibs?" Nibs answered the same way, and so did the other boys until Hook

25
00:02:07.507 --> 00:02:12.738
interrupted. "Tie her up to the mast!" he shouted

26
00:02:12.739 --> 00:02:15.339
cruelly. It was Smee who tied

27
00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:21.726
Wendy. Under his breath, he whispered, "I’ll save you if you promise to be my

28
00:02:21.727 --> 00:02:26.052
mother." But this was a promise Wendy could never make to a pirate.

29
00:02:26.053 --> 00:02:35.353
The boys’ eyes had drifted from Wendy to the plank, and their faces went white. They were not ready to die.

30
00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:43.566
Their walk down the narrow board and over the end into the cold sea would be the last walk they would ever take.

31
00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:49.354
They shivered and stared, no longer sure they could walk the plank as gentlemen.

32
00:02:49.355 --> 00:02:54.100
They were, after all, only little boys.

33
00:02:54.101 --> 00:02:57.792
Hook smiled and took a step toward Wendy.

34
00:02:57.793 --> 00:03:02.589
He wanted to turn her face to make her watch the boys walk the plank.

35
00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:06.301
He wanted to hear her cries of terror and regret.

36
00:03:06.302 --> 00:03:11.535
Instead, what he heard filled his own heart with terror.

37
00:03:11.536 --> 00:03:15.580
It was the tick-tock of the crocodile.

38
00:03:15.581 --> 00:03:21.931
They all heard it—Hook, the other pirates, the boys, and Wendy.

39
00:03:21.932 --> 00:03:28.020
Instantly, they all looked—but not at the water where the sound was coming from.

40
00:03:28.021 --> 00:03:31.561
All their eyes were fixed on Captain Hook.

41
00:03:31.562 --> 00:03:37.741
The crocodile, Hook knew, had only one victim in mind—him!

42
00:03:37.742 --> 00:03:41.761
He fell to the floor, trembling in a heap.

43
00:03:41.762 --> 00:03:46.535
The ticking grew louder, as if the crocodile were getting closer.

44
00:03:46.536 --> 00:03:52.066
Hook crawled on his knees to the other side of the ship, away from the boys and Wendy.

45
00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:55.226
The awful sound was getting even louder.

46
00:03:55.227 --> 00:04:01.563
All Hook could imagine was the terrible crocodile climbing aboard his ship.

47
00:04:01.564 --> 00:04:07.752
"Hide me!" Hook cried, but his men stepped back to clear the way.

48
00:04:07.753 --> 00:04:15.361
They had always been loyal to their captain, but none of them would stand between him and his fate.

49
00:04:15.362 --> 00:04:21.865
On the other side of the deck, the boys leaned over the side of the ship to see the crocodile climb in.

50
00:04:21.866 --> 00:04:27.200
But to their surprise, it was not the crocodile coming to their rescue.

51
00:04:27.201 --> 00:04:39.767
It was Peter! He made a sign for them to keep silent. Then he went on ticking.

